This read-only independent review binds the frozen 145-file Position/Range/Selection candidate at manifest SHA 8e423a7d82ea58c696f9bc3d91f6d3df460c51a2041cbcdcc87d2806c0997ee5 and runtime SHA 7ad0b5ebb78ea575ca381551b7f827776523c606d9a481801f0eb34a67e2f1c1. No author stage, Studio or public repository file was changed.

The independent TypeScript AST census authenticates the VS Code 1.140.0 commit declarations and confirms 30 direct entries and six nested optional fields. It finds an accounting error: Selection inherits ten non-constructor Range declaration entries, with nine distinct member names. The author's count of twelve includes the two Range constructors, while Selection's own constructors are already in its five direct entries. The authored 240-pair corpus is a differently seeded/shaped author corpus; this review does not accept its label as independent held-out evidence.

The fresh reviewer-designed corpus uses its own observation code, not the author's packet or test program. Thirteen finite groups complete with twelve passing and one failing, source-stable, no skips. It records 173 exact paired semantic observations, six unequal legacy-helper observations and nine separate readonly-accessor checks. Readonly values/descriptors/error types agree, but nine raw engine messages have different realm receiver labels; these are retained without normalizing them or counting them as exact message matches.

The confirmed behavioral gap is outside the 30 documented entries. The exact released ES5 compatibility decorator installs ordinary, constructible call/apply functions. The candidate installs shorthand methods, which are not constructible. Reflect.construct on each class's call/apply succeeds originally and throws TypeError in the candidate: six concrete mismatches. Ordinary legacy calls and applies pass. This gap does not establish a failure of the documented Position/Range/Selection surface, and it must not be silently called a match.

Two independent original realms each evaluate five authenticated source units and six VM scripts. This review uses the existing authenticated official TypeScript 5.9.3 parser/compiler through an AST import/export composition and its decorator/type erasure, a separate path from the author's Node stripTypeScriptTypes oracle. Exact transformed execution sources are retained. Ten source-unit evaluations and twelve VM evaluations occur. Two negative provenance gates reject a corrupted source and incorrect Node SHA before any original VM unit executes. Node v24.16.0 and its exact 92,279,112-byte SHA are authenticated before evaluation. No original native program, workbench, extension host or GUI executes.

The 482 role dispatch tallies per role combine grouped scenarios and explicit constructors. They are not a census of original API method/getter/internal calls. The foreign-realm case constructs two opposite-role positions in each role; the equal totals do not remove that disclosed crossover. The author campaigns remain separate: their final 986 packets and 45,117 harness dispatches per role were not replayed here.

The owned direct child exits with code 1 because the legacy-helper comparison fails. Raw output, observations, test/oracle/source snapshots and before/after authority are preserved. The source/Node negative gates pass and the owned negative mirror is removed. Bounds are a 60-second direct-child deadline, 256 MiB old space, 1 MiB stdout/stderr and an 8 MiB prospective observation cap. No hard RSS limit, descendant isolation or fingerprint-I/O deadline is claimed. There are no browser tabs or HTTP hosts. The denied delegation attempt and read-only filename discovery errors are recorded as tooling events, not implementation failures.

The finite documented behavior checks found no confirmed mismatch. Acceptance of the full advertised scope remains pending the denominator correction and explicit treatment of the non-documented helper gap. Full extension API/workbench/product parity, universal adversarial semantics, security equivalence and superiority remain false. See declaration-audit.json, the retained failing run and review-validation.json for exact evidence; review-manifest.json is the strict owned inventory.
